What is Biochar?
Biochar is a carbon-rich material produced through pyrolysis of biomass such as agricultural waste, wood chips, and manure. It serves as a stable soil amendment that enhances fertility while sequestering carbon for centuries. Beyond agriculture, biochar finds applications in water filtration, construction materials, and industrial processes due to its porous structure and adsorption properties.
